.TH DISASSEMBLE 1 "October 11, 2026" "Vircon32 DevTools 26.04.24" "Vircon32 Development Tools"
.SH NAME
disassemble \- turn a Vircon32 binary back into assembly
.SH SYNOPSIS
.B disassemble
.RB [ \-o
.IR output.asm ]
.RB [ \-b ]
.RB [ \-v ]
.I input.vbin
.br
.B disassemble
.B \-\-help
.br
.B disassemble
.B \-\-version
.SH DESCRIPTION
.B disassemble
reads a VBIN program binary \(em as written by
.BR assemble (1),
or extracted from a cartridge by
.BR unpackrom (1)
\(em and writes the corresponding assembly. Jump and call targets are
given generated label names
.RI ( _label1 ", " _label2 ", ...)." The tool focuses on the program code: data
stored in the binary (strings, tables, embedded files) comes out as the
instructions those words would decode to, and references to it stay as
plain addresses.
.SH OPTIONS
.TP
.BI \-o " output.asm"
Write the assembly to
.IR output.asm .
Without
.BR \-o ,
the output path is the input path with its extension replaced by
.IR .asm .
.TP
.B \-b
Treat the binary as a BIOS, whose code starts at address
.B 0x10000000
instead of the cartridge's
.BR 0x20000000 .
.TP
.B \-v
Verbose: report the output path chosen.
.TP
.B \-\-help
Print a usage summary and exit.
.TP
.B \-\-version
Print the version and author, and exit.
.SH EXIT STATUS
.TP
.B 0
The assembly was written.
.TP
.B 1
Any error, printed as
.IR "disassemble: error: description" .
.SH SEE ALSO
.BR assemble (1),
.BR unpackrom (1)
.SH AUTHOR
The Vircon32 disassembler was written by Javier Carracedo
.RI ( Carra ).
This manual page was written by Matthew Haas for the v32c++ project.
